{"text": "Otto Loewi was a pharmacologist. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Whose discoveries greatly advanced. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The study of chemical communication between nerve cells. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Born in Frankfurt, Germany, in 1873. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He originally hoped. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To study art history. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> However, following his parents advice. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Loewi studied medicine. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At the University of Strasbourg, Germany now part of France. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Although he was qualified as a physician. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He chose to switch. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> From a doctor treating patients. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> To a medical researcher seeking cures. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 1902. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He first met Henry Dale. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In Ernest Starlings laboratory in London. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Where he spent several months. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 1936. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> He and Henry Dale shared. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> The Nobel Prize in Physiology or Medicine. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> After Germany invaded Austria in 1938. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Loewi was forced to leave Austria. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Where he was living at the time. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> Loewi became a research professor. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> At New York Universitys College of Medicine. <break time=\"0.8s\" /> In 1940.", "alignment": {"characters": ["O", "t", "t", "o", " ", "L", "o", "e", "w", "i", " ", "w", "a", "s", " ", "a", " ", "p", "h", "a", "r", "m", "a", "c", "o", "l", "o", "g", "i", "s", "t", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=", "\"", "0", ".", "8", "s", "\"", " ", "/", ">", " ", "W", "h", "o", "s", "e", " ", "d", "i", "s", "c", "o", "v", "e", "r", "i", "e", "s", " ", "g", "r", "e", "a", "t", "l", "y", " ", "a", "d", "v", "a", "n", "c", "e", "d", ".", " ", "<", "b", "r", "e", "a", "k", " ", "t", "i", "m", "e", "=